.nh
.TH "GHPM" "1" "Nov 2026" "ghpm" "ghpm manual"

.SH NAME
ghpm-web - Serve a local browser interface


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBghpm web [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a small HTTP server and serves a browser UI for the configured apps.

.PP
The server binds to loopback by default, rejects requests with non-loopback
Host headers, and only accepts JSON writes. Pass --allow-remote to lift those
restrictions (place it behind a reverse proxy with authentication if you do).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--allow-remote\fP[=false]
	accept non-loopback requests

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for web

.PP
\fB--listen\fP="127.0.0.1:8787"
	address to listen on (127.0.0.1:8787)

.PP
\fB--open\fP[=false]
	open the interface in the default browser


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default ~/.config/ghpm/config.yaml)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine readable output (where supported)

.PP
\fB--no-cache\fP[=false]
	bypass the release metadata cache

.PP
\fB--proxy\fP=""
	HTTP(S) proxy URL, overrides config


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBghpm(1)\fP
